    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help---Marketing-Assistant_R0088762": {
      "title": "Extra Help / Marketing Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-22\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the   Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: ASBTDC Department's Website: asbtdc.org Summary of Job Duties: The Extra Help/Marketing Assistant designs graphics and creates media to support ASBTDC’s traditional and digital marketing efforts. The position also contributes to special projects and events to fulfill the goals and strategic initiatives of the organization. The ideal candidate will be a creative and skilled graphic artist who produces professional-caliber work using a wide variety of media techniques. This is an hourly (20 hours per week), grant-funded, non-benefits eligible position. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Formal high school diploma; Portfolio of samples of design work. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Significant secondary coursework or bachelor's degree in art, design, marketing, communications, or related field;  Experience creating graphics for print and digital output; Small business knowledge or work experience; WordPress knowledge or experience; Video editing knowledge or experience. Job Duties and Responsibilities Design Collaborate on conceiving, developing, and designing materials for use in marketing ASBTDC services to Arkansas entrepreneurs and small businesses and educating key stakeholders on the impact of ASBTDC services; Design digital and print pieces, such as flyers, social media images, e-books, banners, presentations, reels, and maps, for ASBTDC marketing and educational purposes; Distill and interpret statistics to produce easy-to-understand charts, infographics, and reports; Apply established brand guidelines, ensuring colors, typography, and logo usage are uniform across all touchpoints; Organize and maintain design files and templates; Ensure files are correctly formatted and print-ready for vendors; Assist ASBTDC staff and offices to fulfill their design requests and meet event and project deadlines. Other Job Duties Contribute to ASBTDC’s brand, visual identity, and messaging; Support organizational marketing, training, and outreach activities; Work cooperatively with staff to provide high-quality service; Maintain confidentiality and adhere to the University System and ASBTDC Conflict of Interest standards; Perform other duties as assigned to accomplish the goals and mission of the organization.   Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite, Canva, Google Workspace, and Microsoft Office Suite; Excellent written and verbal communication skills and the ability to communicate professionally by email, telephone, and face to face; Strong organizational skills and attention to detail; Ability to prioritize and manage multiple projects; Ability to manage multiple assignments and deadlines; Ability to maintain confidentiality. Additional Information: Salary Information: $21/hr Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Other (see special instructions for details), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Samples of design work (minimum of five pieces) Recruitment Contact Information: Gwen Green, ASBTDC Marketing and Communications Manager, gagreen@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: No Background Check Required The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Grasping, Pulling, Pushing, Walking Benefits Eligible: No"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help-Registered-Nurse_R0087523": {
      "title": "Extra Help/Registered Nurse",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-01\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the   Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Health Services Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This position provides the services of an Extra Help/Registered Nurse to the operations of UA Little Rock Health Services. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience Successful completion of an accredited nursing degree   program.   Current licensure as a Registered Nurse by the Arkansas State Board of Nursing or current multistate license from a Nurse Licensure Compact (NLC) member state; Current CPR certification. Job Duties and Responsibilities Provide triage assessments, by telephone and in person, and appropriately direct patients to urgent care, same day, future appointments, and referrals to off-site services as indicated; Urgent care, same day, future appointments, and referrals to off-site services as indicated; Administer medications & immunizations within scope of practice, as ordered by APRNs and MDs, and in accordance with the Arkansas Department of Health (ADH) and Center for Disease Control and Prevention (CDCP) recommendations and standards; Assist receptionist as needed with check-in procedures, making appointments, insurance verification, responding to patient inquiries, and answering the telephone; Provide appropriate and effective health education to patients regarding their health problems, behavioral risk assessment, interventions, and medications; Document all findings and patient care interventions accurately and legibly and according to professional and legal standards; in Medicat (Electronic Health Record); Appropriately refer patients to Advanced Practice Registered Nurses (APRNs), Physicians, and off-site services; Follow client confidentiality policies and procedures for UA Little Rock Health Services and according to HIPAA guidelines; Comply with OSHA and clinic protocols regarding infectious disease prevention and control, including proper handling and disposal of infectious waste, gloving and sharps management/disposal, and proper disinfection of exam rooms and equipment; Maintain and document proper storage of vaccines as per ADH protocols, including completion of daily temperature log for refrigerator and freezer and regular inspection of expiration dates and proper disposal of expired vaccines; Participate and contribute to the development and implementation of campus health outreach programs; Perform CLIA waived tests and collect, package, route, and track lab specimens to off-site reference laboratory as directed; Perform tuberculosis screening and follow-up; including documentation of results in the Arkansas Department of Health tuberculosis database; Participate in regular staff meetings and contribute to progress toward developing and addressing Health Services’ goals and objectives; Participate and contribute to quality improvement programs for Health Services; Participate and contribute to staff in-services and educational programs; Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, And Abilities Knowledge of computers and software applications (Microsoft, Internet, e-mail); Knowledge or ability to learn appropriate use of the Medicat Electronic Health Record system; Strong communication skills to provide effective education to clients and accurately relate client concerns to consulting professionals; Strong ability to work with diverse constituencies including persons with disabilities. Additional Information: Salary Information: Required Documents to Apply: Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Adult Maltreatment, Annual TB Screening, Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Feeling, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Sharps Occasional Physical Activity: Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Pushing Benefits Eligible:"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/Little-Rock/Extra-Help-Police-Officer_R0086937": {
      "title": "Extra Help/Police Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-15\nPart time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: DNU - Public Safety (Inactive) Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the   Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Public Safety Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Extra Help/Police Officer is responsible for the enforcement of traffic, criminal laws and parking regulations. This position is governed by law enforcement standards, state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and experience The formal education equivalent of a high school diploma; Must possess a valid drivers license; Muse be certified by the Arkansas Law Enforcement Certification Training in accordance with ACA 12-9-106, an approved law enforcement training academy. Job Duties and Responsibilities Patrol assigned areas to detect and prevent crimes, enforce traffic laws, recognize parking violations, issue traffic citations, and identify safety hazards and violators; Perform security checks of campus buildings; Conduct investigations of crimes, accidents, and reports incidents committed on campus; Monitor security and fire panel for security and fire detection, assist with checking the alarm systems and emergency power supply, and inspect and maintain fire extinguishers; Arrest violators write incident reports, and testify in court, as required; Direct traffic during periods of high density to facilitate smooth flow; Respond to alarm, call for assistance, check for locked or unlocked buildings and offices, as necessary, and assist stranded motorists and others in need of assistance; Performs other duties as assigned.  Must maintain ACIC (Arkansas Crime Information Center) class one certification. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of general law enforcement methods and techniques; Ability to direct traffic and to maintain order; Ability to prepare reports of incidents and accidents; Ability to communicate orally and in writing; Ability to operate motor vehicles used in patrol duties. Additional Information: Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Physical, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry, and Substance Abuse Testing Salary Information: 15.00 an hour Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Andrea Robinson Police Services Manager 501-916-5308 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to