    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/Little-Rock/Parent-Support-Mentor--Pulaski-County--HEI-Program-Coordinator_R0092300": {
      "title": "Parent Support Mentor (Pulaski County)-HEI Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the   Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: MidSOUTH Department's Website: midsouth.ualr.edu Summary of Job Duties: The Parent Support Mentor is a grant-funded position. This position is located in Pulaski County. The Parent Support Mentor provides training activities and will be a part of a larger team within the county Women Infants & Children (WIC) office. This position will communicate with the grantor and community partners, assist with building training capacity, and collect data for program evaluation. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: High School Diploma or equivalent and (other job-related experience and education may be substituted for all or parts of these basic requirements); ​ Preferred Education and/or Experience: Bachelor's degree; plus one (1) year of specialized training in business management, business education, or a related field.​ Job Duties and Responsibilities: Administrative Coordination: Research and analyze data pertinent to work programs and/or agency/institution goals and objectives and prepare reports explaining findings and recommendations; Assists clients in obtaining pertinent information outlined by the program related to their particular needs and how to fulfill those needs; Teaches and demonstrates health behavior skills to clients; Provide informal education and social skills supports for clients based on identified needs and provide formal educational information based on the Baby and Me curriculum; Coordinate communication between community groups, local health unit supervisor, and program supervisor to ensure everyone receives timely updates of program and/or client changes; Assist in developing or revising policies, procedures, and directives based on research findings and submit to supervisor for approval; Compile program-related information used by the supervisor to formulate budget proposals to determine resources needed and respond to participant correspondence in a timely manner; Review and answer or prepare correspondence relating to agency/institution programs; Interpret agency administrative directives, policies, and procedures to ensure consistent application; Provide information, assistance, and clarifications to interested parties concerning agency/institution programs, policies, and procedures; Recordkeeping : Assist supervisor by maintaining leave records, appointment calendar, and prioritizing incoming correspondence; Travel to other local health units as needed to provide community outreach services; Maintain timely and accurate data in the database using new RedCap software; Submit a weekly work log of day-to-day client activities to Baby and Me Coordinator. Perform related responsibilities as required and assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of the principles and practices of mathematics and statistics; Knowledge of the work-related subject areas; Knowledge of family health and child development; Knowledge of computers and software applications; Ability to prepare, present, and review oral and written information and reports; Ability to work as a part of a team; Ability to research and analyze related work program information; Strong interpersonal and organizational skills; Ability to analyze financial records and prepare reports; Ability to develop, recommend, interpret, and apply policies and procedures; Ability to plan, organize, and direct the work of others; Must have good communication skills; Ability to travel occasionally, as needed; Ability to work a flexible schedule; Ability to work independently. Additional Information: Salary Information: $36,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume, Unofficial/Official Transcript(s) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Mary Tillman, Administrative Support Manager, mjtillman@midsouth.ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Child Maltreatment, Criminal Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Kneeling, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Repetitive Motion Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/Little-Rock/Radio-Membership-Director_R0092297": {
      "title": "Radio Membership Director",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Professional Staff - Institutional Affairs Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the   Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: KLRE/KUAR Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Little Rock Public Radio Membership Director oversees and manages all membership campaigns and fundraising efforts to maintain and expand the membership base of Little Rock Public Radio. The Membership Director reports directly to the Director of Development and coordinates all efforts with the Little Rock Public Radio leadership team. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: Associate’s degree plus two (2) years of experience in nonprofit development, membership, grant writing, for-profit sales, or other revenue-generating position. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Bachelor’s degree in related field; Three (3) or more years of experience in development, marketing, public relations, volunteer management, or a related field. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Design and implement on-air membership campaigns, special events, and community service projects; Design and manage routine solicitations and specialized fundraising projects including but not limited to mid-level gift solicitation, capital campaigns, foundation grants, and planned giving solicitation campaigns by direct mail, email, social media, and telemarketing; and other fundraising projects; Develop and manage donor recognition, gift acknowledgment processes, and member communications, including use of social media; Host live fundraising breaks on the air and voice recorded announcements, as needed; Plan, design and implement special events/projects that provide additional funding, heighten awareness of the stations and/or serve the community in a significant way; Recruit, train and supervise staff and volunteers for membership and fundraising efforts and community outreach projects; Serve as liaison with the Friends of KLRE/KUAR and its Board of Directors, including contacting members, scheduling meetings, helping recruit new Board members, coordinating committee work, and advising the Board; Supervise database management, assuring that station leadership receives timely and meaningful reports;      Work with the station leadership team on strategic planning and setting station policies; Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of philanthropy and fundraising principles; Excellent oral and written communication skills; Strong organizational and interpersonal skills; Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously; Experience in designing and directing events or campaigns; Evidence of supervisory skills; Familiarity with the use of social media for fundraising and outreach; Affinity for public radio; Ability to work occasional nights and weekends; Ability to use a database management system; Ability to work in a website content management system. Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Please upload all required documents in the \"Resume\" attachment section of your application (before hitting the submit button), if you want to be considered for this position. Recruitment Contact Information: Grace Zafasi, Project Coordinator, gzafasi@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/Little-Rock/Faculty-Assistant_R0092153": {
      "title": "Faculty Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Researchers Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the   Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Budget Department's Website: https://ualr.edu/law/ Summary of Job Duties: The Faculty Assistant is responsible for coordinating all general office activities. Responsibilities include purchasing, processing travel and reimbursements, hiring extra labor, tracking faculty budgets, creating and maintaining confidential files, researching and preparing special reports, working on various projects and committees with faculty, and performing other duties as assigned by the supervisor. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: The formal education equivalent of a bachelor's degree. Two years of experience in program administration or related area. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements. Preferred Education and/or Experience: Experience with Google products, including Drive, Sheets, and Docs, Microsoft Office Suite, and Adobe Acrobat Pro. Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations, and procedures preferred. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Serves as an assistant for assigned faculty. Assists in copying, typing, routing, filing, and storing of exams and other documents. Hires extra labor for assigned faculty. May keep appointment calendars and prioritizes incoming correspondence and assignments for assigned faculty. Keeps an up-to-date and accurate record of the budget for assigned faculty and gives them a copy at the beginning of each month. Ensures fax machines, copiers, and printers are maintained and in working order. Maintains paper and office supplies for assigned faculty. Facilitates procurement, travel, and reimbursements by ensuring proper paperwork and forms are completed and submitted in a timely manner, requiring this person to have a purchasing card (P-Card) and a travel card (CTS Card) to make said purchases and travel arrangements. Checks fax machines, e-mails, and voice mails in a timely manner and processes incoming faculty mail. Maintains main supply closet and submits orders to supervisor. Assists with exam and review proctoring, scantron processing, error correction, and response collection. Assists faculty with committee appointments and special projects. Performs annual inventory of the Law School. May assist with travel arrangements, including Workday, for Student Affairs. May assist with hiring student workers in Workday for Student Affairs. May assist with procurement and other miscellaneous Workday tasks for Student Affairs. Will assist with travel arrangements, reimbursements, catering, etc. for all functions related to faculty development, including but not limited to speaker series, luncheons, internal presentations, etc. May serve as back-up for departmental admins when that person is out or the position is vacant.  May require initiating requisitions, travel forms, reimbursements, and other administrative duties as needed. May assist with special projects as needed for the law school. May provide logistical support for college events and meetings as needed. Other duties as assigned by the supervisor. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. Ability and willingness to take initiative in learning and integrating knowledge of office procedures. Strong problem-solving skills. Ability and willingness to integrate guidance and instructions. Ability to manage multiple tasks timely and effectively. Ability to effectively organize and maintain office records and documents. Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. Experience with computers and Microsoft Office suite. Ability to learn campus-based software applications. Effective interpersonal communication both written and oral. Demonstrate patience and accuracy in resolving student, faculty, and staff concerns. Additional Information: Salary Information: $45,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Shanna Fitzgerald, Director of Finance, semorris@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Sitting Frequent Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/Little-Rock/Program-Coordinator_R0092051": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Management, Supervisory Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the   Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Legal Clinic Managing Attorney Department's Website: https://ualr.edu/law/clinical-programs/ Summary of Job Duties: This Program Coordinator with the UA Little Rock Bowen School of Law operates a Legal Clinic, which is a law firm within the law school that provides legal services to low-income Arkansans. The Legal Clinic is staffed by supervising attorneys, and the attorneys work with law students to provide services to clients. The Clinic offers representation in several areas, including family law, tax law, consumer protection, veterans’ benefits, mediation of various types of legal disputes, and advice to small businesses and entrepreneurs. The Program Coordinator is a 12-Month, full-time position that provides administrative support to clinical faculty and programs as assigned by the Associate Dean for Experiential Learning and Clinical Programs and by the Clinic Managing Attorney. The purpose of this position is to provide administrative support in the day-to-day operations of a busy law office held within a University setting as well as execute the vision and direction of the Law School Dean and the Law School Associate Dean for Experiential Learning and Clinical Programs. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience:  The formal education equivalent of a bachelor's degree; Two years of experience in business office practices or program administration; Other job-related education or experience may be substituted for all or parts of these basic requirements. Preferred Education and/or Experience:  Prior work experience as an administrative assistant in a law office; Ability to use law office case-management systems; Qualifications necessary to become certified as a Notary Public. Job Duties and Responsibilities:  Assist the Clinic’s supervising attorneys with their clients and teaching responsibilities; Prepare correspondence and legal documents; Create and maintain client and case files using case-management software; Use case management software to screen new clients for potential conflicts of interest; Prepare and process travel and reimbursement documents for Clinic supervising attorneys and students; Prepare check requests for Clinic supervising attorneys; Prepare applications for students to represent clients under the Arkansas student practice rule; Prepare and mail regular and certified mail; Order office supplies, as needed; Answer clinic telephones, route calls, take messages, check clients in for meetings with supervising attorneys and students; Respond to members of the public who come to the Clinic with walk-in inquiries about legal questions; Compile data and prepares reports from Clio case-management system to document numbers of clients served, cases handled, and students enrolled; Perform monthly reconciliation of clinic's litigation account and IOLTA account; Compile documentation and prepares monthly report for law school budget director on reconciliation of clinic bank accounts; Notarize documents; Assist with the student application and enrollment processes for all clinic, externship, and practicum courses; Assist in maintaining budget spreadsheets and tracking expenditures for clinical programs; Handle other duties as assigned by the Associate Dean for Experiential Learning and Clinical Programs and the Clinic Managing Attorney; Attend applicable trainings to keep up-to-date and improve job performance. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:  Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations, and procedures; Assist in maintaining Clinic office policies and procedures; Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as part of a team; Ability and willingness to take the initiative in learning and integrating knowledge of office procedures; Ability to use Google mail (gmail) and Google docs; Ability to use Clio Legal Practice Management software; Knowledge of office-management practices; Excellent interpersonal communication skills and the ability to conduct all interactions with the public with the utmost civility, professionalism, and empathy; Excellent customer service skills; Excellent written and oral communication skills. Ability to maintain the confidentiality of client and case information; Ability to compile statistics into reports; Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment; Ability to use Microsoft Office suite programs, including Word, Excel, and PowerPoint; Ability to demonstrate patience and accuracy in resolving client, student, faculty, and staff concerns. Additional Information: Salary Information: $45,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Shanna Fitzgerald, Director of Finance, semorris@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Frequent Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/Little-Rock/XMLNAME--HE--Public-Safety-Security-Officer_R0092139": {
      "title": "(HE) Public Safety/Security Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Police and Security Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the   Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Public Safety Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Public Safety/Security Officer provides a variety of security and safety related functions while involved in safeguarding students, faculty, staff, and visitors of the campus. This position provides security for equipment and real property in assigned areas. The Public Safety/Security Officer communicates effectively and respectfully with members of the campus community, supervisors, and peers. This position provides information and directions as needed. May be assigned to a specific zone or geographical work area. Regular, reliable, and non-disruptive attendance is an essential job function of this job, as is the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and Experience Formal education equivalent to a high school diploma; Possession of a valid driver's license. Job Duties and Responsibilitie s Conduct routine checks of campus grounds and buildings to identify unauthorized persons, unauthorized entry, damaged or missing property, and other safety or security concerns; Report observed safety, security, maintenance, or property concerns to the Public Safety Shift Supervisor in a timely manner; Monitor closed-circuit television (CCTV) cameras and alarm systems to identify suspicious activity, unauthorized access, or potential security concerns; Assist students, faculty, staff, and visitors by providing directions, general safety information, and assistance with university and building rules and procedures; Conduct regular foot and vehicle patrols of the Law School, including libraries, lecture halls, administrative offices, and other assigned areas; Inspect doors, windows, and other access points to identify potential security breaches or unsecured areas; Assist with maintaining a safe and orderly environment during routine operations, special events, and emergency situations; Direct traffic as needed to ensure the orderly and safe movement of pedestrians and vehicles; Respond appropriately to emergencies, remain calm under pressure, gather pertinent information, and promptly communicate information to the appropriate Public Safety personnel; Perform other related duties and responsibilities as assigned. Knowledge, Abilities, and Skill s Ability to observe, identify, and report safety and security concerns accurately and promptly; Ability to remain calm and exercise sound judgment during emergencies or other stressful situations; Ability to gather, document, and communicate relevant information effectively; Ability to direct traffic and assist in maintaining order in assigned areas; Ability to operate motor vehicles safely and responsibly; Possession of and ability to maintain a valid driver's license; Ability to communicate effectively and professionally with students, faculty, staff, visitors, supervisors, and coworkers; Ability to work independently and follow established university policies, procedures, and security protocols; Ability to work flexible shifts, including nights, weekends, holidays, and during special events or other periods of increased campus activity. Additional Information: Salary Information: 33,000.00 Required Documents to Apply: Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Andrea Robinson Police Services Manager 501-916-3400 All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, FBI Background Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry, Substance Abuse Testing The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Sitting, Standing, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Lifting, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Pushing, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
