    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-Professor---Metals-and-Jewelry_R0092522": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor / Metals and Jewelry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the   Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: Art and Design Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: This Assistant Professor / Metals and Jewelry position includes the responsibilities of coordinating the metals/jewelry concentration within Applied Design (Ceramics, Metals, Woodworking), which includes teaching metals/jewelry courses, advising and mentoring students, participating in recruitment, retention, special programs, curriculum assessment, and development; maintaining an active scholarship agenda; and contributing to unit, college, and university service. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience: MFA in Metals/Jewelry or related fields. Preferred Education and/or Experience: University-level teaching experience beyond graduate assistantships; Industry experience; Experience with various 3D processes both traditional and digital; A strong record of creative work and evidence of ongoing professional achievement; Experience and commitment to working with diverse populations of learners; Evidence of scholarship related to the position requirements. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching metals/jewelry courses and management of the curriculum; Maintaining an active scholarship agenda; Maintaining the metals studio; Advising students; Supervision of student workers assigned to metals studio; Supervision of adjunct faculty within the metals and jewelry area as needed; Teaching foundation, art appreciation, and other studio disciplines related to training and seminar courses as needed; Working with community and industry partners to provide students with professional skills, job training and career opportunities; Performing other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of various metals/jewelry processes and media; Knowledge of studio safety procedures; Knowledge of computer software related to art, design, and teaching; Demonstrated organizational skills; Ability to teach multiple aspects of metalsmithing and jewelry design; Strong interpersonal skills; Ability to effectively communicate and collaborate; Ability to demonstrate potential for excellence in undergraduate teaching and advising; Willingness to engage in interdisciplinary collaboration with other faculty across the university; Willingness to develop opportunities for engagement with the broader community. Qualification Equivalencies: Additional Information: Salary Information: $61,915 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Other (see special instructions for details) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: In addition to required documents listed above, please submit: -A PDF Portfolio of personal work or link to online portfolio -A PDF Portfolio of Student work or link to online portfolio Recruitment Contact Information: Joli Livaudais, Director, jklivaudais@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Feeling, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Grasping, Hearing, Kneeling, Lifting, Repetitive Motion Occasional Physical Activity: Crouching, Pulling, Pushing, Reaching, Stooping Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/Little-Rock/Assistant-Professor-of-History_R0092525-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of History",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the   Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: History Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Department of History at the University of Arkansas at Little Rock seeks a tenure-track Assistant Professor of History to begin in the fall 2027 semester. Research and teaching expertise should focus on the history of the United States in the nineteenth century. Job duties will include teaching United States history courses in support of the university’s core curriculum, upper-level courses for the department’s robust undergraduate programs, and graduate-level courses in public history as needed. The candidate will also conduct and publish research commensurate with the department’s expectations for tenure and promotion and perform service according to the needs of the department, college, and university. This position is governed by state and federal laws and institutional policies. Qualifications: Required education and experience: Ph.D. in History or related field; ABD applicants may be considered. Preferred education and experience: Prior experience in developing and teaching history courses about the United States during the nineteenth century; Prior experience in developing and teaching asynchronous online courses; A history of community outreach, as UA Little Rock is a community-engaged institution in a metropolitan setting. Job duties and responsibilities: Teach lower-level United States history courses in support of the university’s core curriculum; Teach upper-level or graduate courses for the department’s History major and Public History program; Support the department’s MA program in Public History as a thesis advisor or thesis committee member; Conduct and publish research commensurate with the department’s expectations for tenure and promotion; Perform service according to the needs of the department, college, and university; Participate in community outreach in cooperation with the department, college, and university. Knowledge, skills, and abilities: Demonstrated ability to develop and teach history courses about the United States during the nineteenth century; Demonstrated strong English oral and written communication skills; Self-motivated, responsible, and able to work with minimal direct supervision; Commitment to fostering a sense of belonging and intellectual curiosity in all students. Qualification Equivalencies: Additional Information: Salary Information: $59,000 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Michael Norton, Interim Chair, mbnorton@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Standing, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Pushing, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/Little-Rock/Senior-Director-of-Advancement_R0092656": {
      "title": "Senior Director of Advancement",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Administration - Advancement Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the   Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: VC Advancement Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Senior Director of Advancement of Development is a senior front-line fundraiser responsible for securing significant private philanthropic support for the University of Arkansas at Little Rock. Reporting to the Vice Chancellor for University Advancement, this position develops and manages a portfolio of high-capacity donors and prospects across the University, with a primary emphasis on personally soliciting and closing six- and seven-figure major and principal gifts. The Senior Director of Development advances the University's highest fundraising priorities through donor discovery, strategic cultivation, direct solicitation, and stewardship. Success is measured by substantial gift commitments, growth in the major and principal gift pipeline, and achievement of annual fundraising goals. This position is governed by state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience Bachelor's degree; Demonstrated success personally soliciting and closing gifts and advancing donor relationships toward commitments; Demonstrated ability to meet goals, develop new relationships, and manage complex cultivation and solicitation strategies. Preferred Education and/or Experience At least five years of progressive fundraising experience, including direct responsibility for major gift donor portfolios and personal solicitation. Demonstrated success personally securing six and seven-figure gifts. Experience in comprehensive campaigns, planned giving, and corporate or foundation fundraising. Understanding of large, complex, decentralized public higher education institutions. Master's degree or Certified Fund Raising Executive (CFRE) credential. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Development/Fundraising Personally cultivate, solicit, and close major and principal gifts, with a primary focus on commitments of $100,000 or more and the development of opportunities for gifts of $1 million or more; Build and manage a focused portfolio of high-capacity individuals, alumni, friends, corporations, and foundations whose interests align with University priorities; Identify and personally qualify new prospects, re-engage donors with untapped giving potential, and advance existing relationships toward larger philanthropic commitments; Develop and execute individualized donor strategies with defined gift opportunities, proposed ask amounts, action steps, and timelines for solicitation and closure; Secure support for endowed scholarships, program excellence, academic programs, the living and learning environment, and other strategic University priorities; Conduct a minimum of ten (10) meaningful face-to-face visits weekly with donors and prospects, emphasizing relationships that advance major and principal gift opportunities. Meet annual performance goals established with Advancement leadership for dollars committed, major and principal gift asks and closes, donor visits, and qualified pipeline growth. Fundraising expectations will reflect the senior level of this position and its focus on larger gifts; Lead complex gift solicitations, including commitments involving multiyear pledges, planned gifts, and multiple University priorities, in coordination with appropriate University and Foundation partners; Prepare compelling proposals and coordinate the participation of the Chancellor, Vice Chancellor, deans, faculty, and volunteers in donor cultivation and solicitation; Provide meaningful stewardship that fulfills donor intent, demonstrates the impact of gifts, and creates opportunities for continued and increased support. Administrative Collaborate with Advancement leadership, college development officers, and academic leaders to define fundable priorities and coordinate donor outreach across the University; Partner with Advancement Services on prospect research, portfolio alignment, gift documentation, and stewardship reporting; Maintain timely and accurate donor records, activity reports, proposals, projected gift amounts, and next steps in the donor management system; Prepare donor briefings, solicitation plans, and portfolio reports; regularly review progress toward goals and adjust strategies to advance gifts toward closure; Attend campus, community, and development-related events that support donor relationships and fundraising objectives; Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills, including the ability to make persuasive cases for significant philanthropic investment; Ability to build trust with high-capacity donors and confidently solicit and negotiate substantial gift commitments; Strong judgment, initiative, and organizational skills, with the ability to independently manage complex donor relationships and sustain progress toward ambitious fundraising goals; Ability to work effectively with University leadership, faculty, Advancement colleagues, volunteers, and community partners; Proficiency in preparing donor strategies, proposals, presentations, and gift agreements. Knowledge of major and principal gift fundraising, planned giving vehicles, donor stewardship, and ethical fundraising practices; Flexibility to work evenings, weekends, and holidays as needed; Valid driver's license with the ability to travel in and out of state, including overnight stays. Qualification Equivalencies: Additional Information: Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Christian O'Neal, Vice Chancellor for University Advancement, cxoneal@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Motor Vehicle Reports Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing Frequent Physical Activity: Driving, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Reaching, Sitting, Talking, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Driving, Kneeling, Lifting, Pulling, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS/job/Little-Rock/Administrative-Analyst_R0092407": {
      "title": "Administrative Analyst",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com , then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at University of Arkansas System will also view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students”. All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page.   Closing Date: Type of Position: Clerical Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Day Shift (United States of America) Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas at Little Rock The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is a metropolitan research university that provides an accessible, quality education through flexible learning and unparalleled internship opportunities. At UA Little Rock, we prepare our more than 8,900 students to be innovators and responsible leaders in their fields. Committed to its metropolitan research university mission, UA Little Rock is a driving force in Little Rock's thriving cultural community and a major component of the city and state's growing profile as a regional leader in research, technology transfer, economic development, and job creation. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the   Apply link/button. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 501-916-3180 . Department: College of Humanities Arts, Social Sciences & Education Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The Administrative Analyst is responsible for administrative support in the College of Humanities, Arts, Social Sciences, and Education (CHASSE) Dean’s Office. Administrative duties include but are not limited to college stakeholder communication, paperwork tracking support, financial support, scheduling support, and researching and preparing special reports. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency policy. Qualifications: Required Education and/or Experience Formal education is equivalent to a high school diploma.  Preferred Education and/or Experience Associate’s degree or higher; Experience with Banner, Workday, and/or Degree Works. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Support the work of the Dean’s Office through general duties: support office management and documentation; support communication with internal and external stakeholders; assist with college space needs; support for Mailroom coordination, and support financial activities for the college; Assist the CHASSE Student Success Center with communications to students and other advising-related administrative tasks including communicating with newly admitted students, and coordinating with Mail  assigning advisors and running needed reports on campus systems; Assist with scheduling and course section building in Workday Student; Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated ability to adjust to change and be flexible; Ability to make mature, common-sense decisions based on current and/or available knowledge; Ability to display a cooperative and approachable attitude and demeanor; Knowledge of work-related subject area; Knowledge of computers and software applications and ability to quickly learn platforms to support essential activities; Ability to demonstrate a working knowledge of basic mathematics; Ability to prepare, present, and review oral and written information and reports; Ability to research and analyze related work program information; Ability to develop, recommend, interpret, and apply policies and procedures; Ability to work simultaneously on multiple projects and demonstrate organizational and prioritization abilities in accomplishing tasks. Qualification Equivalencies: Additional Information: Salary Information: $36,327 Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title), Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Recruitment Contact Information: Jeremy Ecke, CHASSE Dean, jsecke@ualr.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Financial Credit Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas at Little Rock is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry ( MVR ) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: Hearing, Manipulate items with fingers, including keyboarding, Sitting, Talking Frequent Physical Activity: Repetitive Motion, Walking Occasional Physical Activity: Lifting, Reaching Benefits Eligible: Yes"
